<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The Play Games Services project id, from the top of the Play Games
      Services page in the Play Console. It is a number, not a package name,
      and it looks like 123456789012.

      The Play Games SDK reads it out of the manifest, so it has to live here
      as a resource rather than in Dart. Until it is real, the game keeps the
      leaderboard screen in its "not set up yet" state and never calls the SDK,
      which is why a placeholder here cannot crash anything.

      The same console also needs the SHA-1 of whichever keystore signed the
      build registered as an OAuth client, debug keystore included, or sign in
      fails on a developer's own phone while working fine from the store.
    -->
    <string name="games_project_id" translatable="false">1026987889374</string>
    <!--
      The achievement ids the same console handed back are not repeated here.
      Nothing on the Android side reads them: the game passes them to the
      plugin from Dart, so they live in lib/services/play_ids.dart and only
      there. Two copies of fifteen ids is two chances for them to drift apart.
    -->
    <!--
      One gotcha worth knowing before the real id goes in: a string resource
      whose whole value is digits can be folded into an integer by the resource
      compiler, and the SDK then rejects it as an invalid app id. If that
      happens, put a backslash and a space in front of the number.
    -->
</resources>
